// expect: 42
// A PARAMETER SPELLED `len` IS TYPED AS THE SEQUENCE OPERATION. `len` is
// `apply`'s parameter, bound to `inc`, so `len(x)` is 42. The program
// refuses with E_TypeMismatch "Int vs List" (measured 2026-09-25): the
// judgment recognizes a sequence operation by the callee's spelling.
//
// Retires when a call is judged by the declaration it resolves to
// (Hβ.resolve.reference-is-an-edge).
fn apply(len, x) = len(x)

fn inc(n) = n + 1

fn main() = apply(inc, 41)
